################################################################################
#### FOR NEXT COMMIT DESCRIPTION ###############################################


Fixed a memory leak when no midi device was found (wrong destruction
order).

Discarded unsupported midi messages, assuring well behavior if
unknown midi messages arrive.

The midi collecion was modified to a handler/hook based interface. In
this way every game/excercise can register a handler to a midi message
type (only tone on/off are supported but the designe is prett
scalable. Default handlers for midi tone on/off events were added,
they just print messages like:
	"Channel '4' just pressed the 'do' (semitone 0 in octave)
	in the '4' octave with '26' velocity"
	"Channel '4' just released the 'do' (semitone 0 in octave)
	in the '4' octave with '0' velocity





FIX Refactorization, better encapsulation

New stuctures were created for midi and the guess_note game to store
members previously located in the main pt struct. Creator and
destroyer functions were written for this new structs and the ones
for pt were modified accordingly.

Slowly improving the old midi, but not yet re-designed. It almost
works as I wanted, but it's not written as I want it.

Lot's of known leaks (I just wanted to play a little).




More user interface experiments just to play with the following
functions I need for another project:
	From unistd.h or C standard library"
		isatty
		ttyname
		tcsetattr
		tcgetattr
		ttyslot
		ioctl
	From termcap library:
		tgetent
		tgetflag
		tgetnum
		tgetstr
		tgoto
		tputs


